  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a function defined as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"center left\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mpadded lspace=\"-1px\"><mi>if</mi></mpadded><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> is equal to :</p>"
  },
